<p>Michael did it again. Twelve wins, second ring in three years, and the fattest
single-season payday this league has ever handed out. But the season belonged to
the guy who finished last.</p>

<h3><span class="n">§</span> The Robbed</h3>
<p>Richard.</p>
<div class="decree">Richard scored 1,711.20 points in 2025 — third-most in the
league — and finished 4-11, dead last.</div>
<p>His Week 15 was a top-three score in the league that week, and a loss. He scored
like a contender and finished dead last, and it is not close.</p>

<h3><span class="n">§</span> The Fraud</h3>
<p>Jeremy went 10-5, luckier than the standings let on, and David wasn't far behind
at 9-6. Both of them finished ahead of a Richard team that outscored them by a
country mile.</p>

<h3><span class="n">§</span> The Weird</h3>
<p>Bates named his team "Carried by Gibbs*," with the asterisk, then went out and
got carried by Gibbs to a runner-up finish — <span class="stat">49.90</span> in
Week 12 alone. Justin benched Jared Goff for <span class="stat">43.96</span>, which
is becoming a Goff-shaped tradition around here. Cory ran a team named "Scheisse,"
went 5-10, and won <span class="stat">$0</span>, which is the correct amount.</p>

<h3><span class="n">§</span> The Bench Problems</h3>
<p>Dylan left plenty on the table all year and still took a hundred dollars home
for it somehow. Sam scored the least of anybody. Nobody was surprised.</p>

<div class="respect"><p class="crown">The Champion</p><p>Michael went 12-3 with a
six-game win streak, second ring in three years, and cleared
<span class="stat">$1325</span> — the richest single season on record.</p></div>

<p>Michael took the biggest check anyone's ever taken. Richard scored the
third-most points in the league and left with <span class="stat">$200</span> and a
grievance he'll be airing for a decade.</p>
